    <fr:title text="The degree law">The degree law</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p><fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \deg  \kappa (U_{n}) = \lfloor  n(n+6)/12 \rfloor ,
]]></fr:tex>
with equality in the modality cap: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\deg  \kappa (U_{n}) = (n-1) + \operatorname {mod}(B : \mathfrak {n}_{n})]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> The lower bound is a theorem, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0037/" title="The growth theorem" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/" display-uri="ffi-0037" type="local">the growth theorem</fr:link>;
the upper bound is <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0029/" title="Theorem D: the modality cap" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0029/" display-uri="ffi-0029" type="local">Theorem D</fr:link>; what is conjectural is that they
meet. Both sides are known for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex>. For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 10 \dots  16]]></fr:tex> the
resulting lower bounds on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {mod}(B : \mathfrak {n}_{n})]]></fr:tex> — from 4 up to 14 — are
unconditional, using VLA 2003, GMR 2014 and the Pak--Soffer Appendix A
degrees. Verified <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  16]]></fr:tex>; the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 17]]></fr:tex> prediction (degree 32) runs
ahead of the literature.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0026/" title="The class count kappa(U_n)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0026/" display-uri="ffi-0026" type="local">The class count kappa(U_n)</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0029/" title="Theorem D: the modality cap" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0029/" display-uri="ffi-0029" type="local">Theorem D: the modality cap</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0037/" title="The growth theorem" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/" display-uri="ffi-0037" type="local">The growth theorem</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p>
      <html:em>Provenance: lc_law.md Theorem C/D; scratch_nineteenth.md for the
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  17]]></fr:tex> table.</html:em>
    </html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
